     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Saturday, November 23, 2013 2:23:32 PM UTC-5, Bob Carpenter wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Thanks for the detailed report.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>Indeed, gcc 4.1 is too old.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>We&#39;ve only tested Linux with gcc versions 4.4 to 4.7.\r\n<br>We know Stan requires at least 4.2.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>Ben --- have you tested gcc 4.8?  That&#39;s the latest\r\n<br>stable version.  GNU itself only supports back\r\n<br>to version 4.7:\r\n<br>\r\n<br>   <a href=\"http://www.google.com/url?q=http%3A%2F%2Fgcc.gnu.org&amp;sa=D&amp;sntz=1&amp;usg=AFQjCNEHO42-Jswmc3e0PHYqpVEYHfr_ig\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.google.com/url?q%3Dhttp%253A%252F%252Fgcc.gnu.org%26sa%3DD%26sntz%3D1%26usg%3DAFQjCNEHO42-Jswmc3e0PHYqpVEYHfr_ig&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467485549000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Xp-M7mH8b3XoD6cNaqL-Y\">http://gcc.gnu.org</a>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>- Bob\r\n<br>\r\n<br>On 11/23/13, 1:53 PM, Timothï¿½e Flutre wrote:\r\n<br>&gt; I followed step by step the instructions &lt;<a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fstan-dev%2Frstan%2Fwiki%2FRStan-Getting-Started&amp;sa=D&amp;sntz=1&amp;usg=AFQjCNGNZl-BzmWBmHsw3f5EgzbvO0p-0w\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.google.com/url?q%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Fgithub.com%252Fstan-dev%252Frstan%252Fwiki%252FRStan-Getting-Started%26sa%3DD%26sntz%3D1%26usg%3DAFQjCNGNZl-BzmWBmHsw3f5EgzbvO0p-0w&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792467485549000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1qKV-cNwKpQlGLf-AJNG0u\">https://github.com/stan-dev/rstan/wiki/RStan-Getting-Started</a>&gt; but got the\r\n<br>&gt; message &quot;compilation failed&quot;:\r\n<br>&gt; |\r\n<br>&gt; install.packages(&#39;inline&#39;)\r\n<br>&gt; install.packages(&#39;Rcpp&#39;)\r\n<br>&gt; library(inline)\r\n<br>&gt; library(Rc